# MVP Budget & Infrastructure Constraints

Target: Azure Container Apps (scale-to-zero) + Azure SQL Basic or Postgres free tier.

## Cold Starts

- Keep application startup under ~1 second.
- Avoid heavy runtime reflection, service locator patterns, expensive startup tasks.
- Minimize DI registrations and middleware in the hot path.

## Health Checks (Critical)

- `/health` must be **in-memory only** — no database pings.
- Do NOT add DB queries to Liveness or Readiness probes.
- Continuous health-check DB pings prevent Azure SQL Serverless auto-pause and exhaust Basic DTU.

## Logging & Telemetry

```csharp
builder.Logging.AddFilter("Microsoft", LogLevel.Warning);
builder.Logging.AddFilter("System", LogLevel.Warning);
builder.Logging.AddFilter("System.Net.Http", LogLevel.Warning);
// App namespace at Information only
builder.Logging.AddFilter("juskel", LogLevel.Information);
```

Stay under Application Insights 5 GB/month free ingestion quota.

## Database

- Use `AddDbContextPool` instead of `AddDbContext`.
- Pass `CancellationToken` on all async DB calls.
- Select only required columns; avoid `SELECT *`.
